# phase1/admin/.htaccess
# W-04 Fix — Server-side protection for /admin/ directory
#
# PREVIOUS STATE (HIGH — W-04):
#   Admin panel HTML pages were publicly accessible by URL.
#   Security relied entirely on client-side JS redirects — which are
#   not a security control. Any user could access /admin/dashboard.html
#   directly by typing the URL.
#
# CURRENT STATE:
#   All /admin/ requests are blocked at the web server level.
#   A 403 Forbidden is returned before any HTML is served.
#   This eliminates the exposure while the real solution (NestJS
#   server-rendered admin behind JWT auth) is built in Phase 3.
#
# DEPLOYMENT:
#   Apache: Place this file at /admin/.htaccess on your server
#   Nginx:  Use the nginx.conf snippet in this same folder instead
#
# ─── Apache (.htaccess) ─────────────────────────────────────────────

# Block all direct browser access to admin pages
Order Deny,Allow
Deny from all

# If your hosting uses mod_authz_core (Apache 2.4+), use this instead:
# <RequireAll>
#   Require all denied
# </RequireAll>
